      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s often not useful to say what previous code did, since that code does not exist any more. Instead, we could say something like the following:\n\n    // Note that if |request| did not come from mPendingTetheringRequests, remove()\n    // will have no effect. Requests must not remain hanging in mPendingTetheringRequests,\n    // because if they did, fuzzy-matching would prevent enabling tethering until\n    // someone calls stopTethering or the device is rebooted. However, this cannot\n    // happen because requests can fail to match only in the following cases:\n    //\n    // 1. getOrCreatePendingTetheringRequest does not find a request with the given\n    //    type and returns a placeholder.\n    // 2. tetherInternal is being called from legacyTether.\n    // 3. P2P or LOHS connect\n    // 4. There\u0027s an IP conflict on TETHERING_VIRTUAL.\n    //\n    // #1 and #2 are not a problem: it\u0027s OK that remove() will not do anything, because\n    // there is nothing to remove.\n    // #3 and #4 are also OK: P2P, LOHS and virtual tethering don\u0027t keep requests in\n    // mPendingTetheringRequests, so there is nothing to remove.",
